@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Test retry — preserved snapshot versus stale/new request
hide footbox
autonumber
participant "FrancAnalyzer / api.ts" as UI
participant "analyzer_api.record_test()" as API
participant "require_shared_grammar()\npublic_access.py" as Guard
participant "analyzer_history.record_test()" as History
participant "store : PublicWorkspaceStore" as Store
activate UI
UI -> API : POST /api/analyzer/tests\nsame pending UUID, text and grammar
activate API
note over API : Origin/CSRF/limits passed; shared lock is held.\nA curator may have changed the saved grammar since the first attempt.
API -> Guard : require_shared_grammar(grammar, request_id)
activate Guard
Guard -> Store : load_coursework() via load_project()
activate Store
Store --> Guard : current saved grammar
deactivate Store
opt submitted grammar differs from current saved grammar
  Guard -> Store : load_analyzer_request(request_id)
  activate Store
  Store --> Guard : earlier snapshot, or None
  deactivate Store
end
Guard --> API : allow current grammar or existing request;\notherwise 409 reload required
deactivate Guard
opt grammar guard allowed this request
  API -> History : record_test(request)
  activate History
  History -> Store : load_analyzer_request(request_id)
  activate Store
  Store --> History : earlier RecordedTest, or None
  deactivate Store
  alt prior snapshot has identical text and grammar_source
    note over History : Return that exact earlier snapshot; no compiler run or insert.\nThis remains valid after an offline grammar change.
  else prior snapshot has different text or grammar_source
    note over History : Raise CollectionError(409); do not replace the original.
  else no prior snapshot and current grammar matched
    note over History : Run the normal new-test workflow on sequence-analyzer-test.
  end
  History --> API : original/new snapshot, or explicit 409
  deactivate History
end
API --> UI : result, or 409 with reload/conflict guidance
deactivate API
note over UI : Success clears pendingTest. A retryable interruption keeps it.\nAfter a successful run, pressing Analyze again intentionally uses a new UUID.
deactivate UI
legend bottom
  Stable PUBLIC_OWNER_ID makes retry lookup survive cookie changes; it is not a fabricated account.
  Public request IDs are idempotency keys, not credentials. Exact payload comparison prevents key reuse from overwriting data.
  A new stale request fails before analysis; existence alone does not bypass the later exact-payload check.
endlegend
@enduml
